Added :meth:`StrEnum.get() <icalendar.enums.StrEnum.get>`, which returns the member with the given value, or ``None`` or a default value if no member has that value, without raising :class:`ValueError`. The lookup is case-insensitive. This is available on all enums, for example ``PARTSTAT.get("ACCEPTED")``. AI-assisted: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code was used as a tutor for my code review, writing tests and for proper docstrings. I reviewed and verified the final changes. @FeJo5952